{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed to Gerrit for review — change **2455**: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2455 (commit 94ea939daafc, Change-Id I4fe839b585e61d3beb0677c1423ad66b0659e8c9). Ticket stays in_progress; awaiting `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1` before close.\n\nFiles (7 changed, +658):\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — activate + route `project.failure-disposition-contract`: exec 1-TURN, facet project-invariants, scope container+leaf, default_posture advisory (never blocks), block_threshold 0.9, two checklist sub-answers (affects_failure_disposition GATE, disposition_contract_stated REQ). NO `trigger` (no DET detector in v1 — LLM-judged applicability, like necessity). NO `suppress_types`.\n- `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-failure-disposition-contract.md` — single-turn rubric; explicit T5b anti-double-flag clause; rebar disposition vocab (INDETERMINATE/WAIT_AND_RETRY/NEEDS_INVESTIGATION/exit-11/classify_llm_failure/should_fall_back).\n- `.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-failure-disposition-contract.eval.yaml` — bounded hand-authored 7-case sanity corpus (FIRE: FDC-TP1 config-flip fallback no-winner, FDC-TP2 single-arm exception no-disposition, FDC-TP3 fallback masks retryable primary; PASS: FDC-TN1 full contract stated, FDC-TN2 non-failure \"fallback\" sense, FDC-TN3 doc/test-only, FDC-TN4 T5b-orthogonal new call with per-arm disposition). NOT a batch eval.\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/failure_disposition_sanity.json` — frozen operator-attested expected baseline (recall 1.0 / false-accept 0.0).\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md` — new \"An advisory failure-disposition guard\" dogfood subsection.\n- `tests/unit/test_project_failure_disposition_contract.py` — offline (no-LLM) pins: registration/routing/rubric/eval-shape/calibration-under-perfect-solve/baseline, and the escalated-bug-routes-it / light-bug-tier-does-not behavior (the ticket's \"verify this\" clause).\n- `.gitignore` — surgically un-ignore the two new committed overlay files (`.rebar/prompts/*` and `.rebar/evals/*` are ignored by default).\n\nEvidence: RED first (11 failed — unknown criterion / missing overlay files), then GREEN (14 passed) after creating the overlay. `make lint` + `make typecheck` pass; the criterion/eval/routing regression cluster (test_new_eval_specs, test_criteria_snapshot, test_criteria_eval, test_criterion_preview, plan_review/test_criteria_blocking, test_code_review_criteria_routing, plus necessity + portability) all pass. Commit carries the `rebar-ticket: c789-e1bb-4c7b-496c` trailer + DCO sign-off; `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` = OK.\n\nDesign constraints honored: advisory (never blocking); NOT added to registry.BUG_TIER_CRITERIA; no `suppress_types:[\"bug\"]`; no new external dependency; no new DET detector. Two blocking review-plan findings were resolved before claim (DET P1/P10 heading+testing; E6/F1 AC-split) — attestation PASS + signed, bound to origin/main 5c28ce66."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788145375379252992,"uuid":"cefed49d-b65d-4443-8e71-6a80c487be53"}